    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An Omani Arab sultanate on Zanzibar and Pemba, separated from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#oman">Oman</a> when Sayyid Said’s realm was divided in 1856.</li><li>Clove plantations, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ivory-trade">ivory</a> caravans and the slave market made Zanzibar the commercial capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#east-africa">East Africa</a>.</li><li>European partition stripped its mainland claims; it became a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1890 and fell in the revolution of 1964.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Anglo-Zanzibar War of 27 August 1896 is often called the shortest war in recorded history: the British bombardment of the sultan’s palace lasted less than an hour.</p></aside>
    </section>

